- One `ci.yml` workflow on pull requests and pushes to `main`, with every action pinned to a commit SHA and its version in a comment, and Dependabot for updates.
- Jobs for the Gradle build, lint and unit tests, and for instrumented tests on an emulator. GitHub's Ubuntu runners need a udev rule before the emulator can use KVM ([android-emulator-runner](https://github.com/ReactiveCircus/android-emulator-runner)).
- The app has its own version, independent of Tokkl's, with its own `v*` tags and changelog, starting at 0.1.0. semantic-release does not support a first release below 1.0.0 ([FAQ](https://semantic-release.gitbook.io/semantic-release/support/faq)), so the first release is a hand-made `v0.1.0` tag and semantic-release counts on from it. A commit marked as a breaking change then moves the app to 1.0.0.
9-These steps prepare a Linux x86_64 machine to build and test the app. Everything installs under `$HOME` and needs no root.
14-| Android SDK Command-line Tools | 23.0 | `~/Android/Sdk/cmdline-tools/latest` |
21-The Gradle wrapper downloads Gradle 9.8.1 and checks it against the SHA-256 sum in `gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties`. `gradle/libs.versions.toml` sets Android Gradle Plugin 9.4.1, Kotlin 2.4.21 and Compose BOM 2026.09.00. The app compiles against API 37, which Compose UI 1.12 and androidx.core 1.19 require. It targets API 36, the API level of the test emulator. Android Gradle Plugin 9.4 uses Build-Tools 36.0.0 by default.
23-Android Gradle Plugin 9.4 needs JDK 17 or later, and JDK 21 is an LTS release above that floor. The system image is the plain AOSP build of Android 16 (API 36), not a Google APIs or Play Store build. It keeps SystemUI and the launcher, which tests of the notification, the Quick Settings tile and the widget need. The smaller Automated Test Device images remove both.
